# Context and handoff contract

The context rules for every role that sends work to another agent or
picks up work from one: what a packet must carry, what a reply must
cite, and how an interrupted bout is resumed. Its premise is that the
target knows only its baseline instructions plus what the packet
supplies.

## Packets are self-contained

A handoff packet carries its own world: objective, current state
(artifacts, assumptions, prior results), design and constraints, the
exact task, and the output required. Nothing essential lives only in the
sender's conversation history. Assume no memory of earlier exchanges
between the two roles; if a fact matters, it is in the packet.

## Cite durable paths, do not duplicate

When a result is too large or too central to inline, hand over a durable
path, not the body: an artifact or file path, a run receipt, or a result
address. A citation names the exact version or location; a copy that
drifts is worse than a pointer. The same rule runs the other way —
consume context from cited paths rather than asking another agent to
restate what it already wrote down.

## Reconciliation before handoff

Trigger: a correction was made mid-bout and a decision-facing
deliverable or packet is about to leave. Reconcile it against the bout's
authoritative request and final corrected state, and propagate the
correction into every artifact still carrying the pre-correction
statement. Scope: decision-facing deliverables and packets only, not
scratch. <!-- v7: P-1, P-2, P-5 -->

## Work-order format

Each delegated unit of work is a work order in the packet shape:
objective, current state, design, task, output required. It names the
deliverable before the work runs and states what will count as
acceptance, so the receiver can stop when the criteria are met.

## Resume packets

An interrupted bout is resumed from a resume packet: what was done, what
the evidence showed, what remains, and the paths needed to continue —
not from memory or from scrolling a transcript. Ending a bout without
one loses the work; a traceless bout is a failed handoff to your future
self.

## Reply sentinel from discovery roles

A search brief may return exactly NO_SEARCH_NEEDED: no targeted search
was required for this request. That is a valid completion — not an error,
not a failure, and not an empty result. Callers consume it as-is: do not
re-dispatch the same request to the searcher or another discovery role on
the strength of the sentinel alone. The staged pipeline's search stage is
one consumer of this rule; every direct caller is bound by it the same
way.

## Mission artifact layout

The layout for mission-scoped artifacts is defined by the route
configuration; this contract states only that mission artifacts are
cited by their durable path, as above.
